        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: delete dead infra and config exports",
        "body": "Related: #105595\n\nAI-assisted: implemented and reviewed with Codex.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe enforced production-mode Knip ratchet still carried 593 dead-export entries under `src/config` (214) and `src/infra` (379). Those exports unnecessarily enlarged internal module surfaces and kept tests coupled to code that production never imports.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis removes export modifiers where implementations remain useful internally, deletes code and tests that existed only for dead exports, and keeps production/config contracts that are consumed by runtime callers, schema generation, or documented surfaces. Tests retained for meaningful behavior now exercise production APIs instead of re-exported test helpers. The dead-export baseline was regenerated from current `main` immediately before the final push.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended runtime or config behavior change. The internal TypeScript surface is smaller, dead test-only code is gone, and the enforced baseline drops every `src/config` and `src/infra` entry so future regressions are blocked by CI.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Final head: `cc4aa00cb34c30b0f25c23198228f0d61351f238`; merge base: `5cd1d13493757ff294cda9fc64c991e3b02fc0f7`.\n- Final production-mode baseline: 3,480 entries; SHA-256 `5f2c54dfa965dba18a8d9064317e7242cea9306490d6ff269e6820b39369631e`; zero entries begin with `src/config/` or `src/infra/`.\n- Testbox `tbx_01kxd6g4s4rjtpgmhgkdqbj3qn` passed `pnpm deadcode:exports:update`, `pnpm deadcode:exports`, `pnpm tsgo:prod`, `pnpm tsgo:scripts`, `pnpm tsgo:test`, `pnpm check:architecture`, `pnpm build`, the session-accessor boundary guard, and 465 focused tests across infra, gateway run-loop, ACP command dispatch, and auto-reply before the final clean rebase.\n- After rebasing to current `main`, `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs --update` and `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs` passed on the final head. Testbox refresh was unavailable because Blacksmith workflow fetches returned HTTP 429 and the fallback coordinators were at shared owner capacity (11/10).\n- Conflict-affected focused fallback: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/clawhub.test.ts src/security/windows-acl.test.ts` passed 71/71 tests.\n- The final lint-only follow-up matches current `main`'s workshop import formatting; the dead-export verifier passed again on the pushed head.\n- Autoreview: coherent implementation, integration, and repair slices completed with no accepted/actionable findings; the final Windows preservation patch was rated correct (0.92).\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n",
